Stryker: Stryker mutator for .Net

Stryker mutator for .Net

Usage: Stryker [command] [options]

Options:
  -f|--config-file <relative-path>    Choose the file containing your stryker
                                      configuration relative to current working
                                      directory. Supports json and yaml formats.
                                      | default: stryker-config.json

  -b|--break-at <0-100>               Anything below this mutation score will
                                      return a non-zero exit code. Must be less
                                      than or equal to threshold low. | default:
                                      '0' | allowed: 0 - 100

  --threshold-high <0-100>            Minimum good mutation score. Must be
                                      higher than or equal to threshold low. |
                                      default: '80' | allowed: 0 - 100

  --threshold-low <0-100>             Minimum acceptable mutation score. Must be
                                      less than or equal to threshold high and
                                      more than or equal to threshold break. |
                                      default: '60' | allowed: 0 - 100

  -L|--log-to-file                    Makes the logger write to a file. Logging
                                      to file always uses loglevel trace. |
                                      default: 'False'

  -V|--verbosity                      The verbosity (loglevel) for output to the
                                      console. | default: 'info' | allowed:
                                      error, warning, info, debug, trace

  -c|--concurrency <number>           By default Stryker tries to make the most
                                      of your CPU, by spawning as many parallel
                                      processes as you have CPU cores.
                                      This setting allows you to override this
                                      default behavior.
                                      Reasons you might want to lower this
                                      setting:
                                      
                                      - Your test runner starts a browser
                                      (another CPU-intensive process)
                                      - You're running on a shared server
                                      - You are running stryker in the
                                      background while doing other work |
                                      default: '10'

  --disable-bail                      Disable abort unit testrun as soon as the
                                      first unit test fails. | default: 'False'


Build options:
  -s|--solution <file-path>           Full path to your solution file. Required
                                      on dotnet framework.

  --configuration <Release,Debug>     Configuration to use when building the
                                      project(s) (e.g., 'Debug' or 'Release').
                                      If not specified, the default
                                      configuration of the project(s) will be
                                      used.

  -p|--project <project-name.csproj>  Used to find the project to test in the
                                      project references of the test project.
                                      Example: "ExampleProject.csproj" |
                                      default: ''

  -tp|--test-project                  Specify the test projects. | default: []

  --msbuild-path                      The path to the msbuild executable to use
                                      to build your .NET Framework application.
                                      Not used for .net (core).

  --target-framework                  The framework to build the project
                                      against.


Mutation options:
  -m|--mutate <glob-pattern>          Allows to specify file that should in- or
                                      excluded for the mutations.
                                      Use glob syntax for wildcards:
                                      https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glob_(programming)
                                      Use '!' at the start of a pattern to
                                      exclude all matched files.
                                      Use '{<start>..<end>}' at the end of a
                                      pattern to specify spans of text in files
                                      to in- or exclude.
                                      Example:
                                      ['**/*Service.cs','!**/MySpecialService.cs',
                                      '**/MyOtherService.cs{1..10}{32..45}'] |
                                      default: ['**/*']

  -l|--mutation-level                 Specify which mutation levels to place.
                                      Every higher level includes the mutations
                                      from the lower levels. | default:
                                      'Standard' | allowed: Basic, Standard,
                                      Advanced, Complete

  --since[:<committish>]              Enables diff compare. Only test changed
                                      files. | default: 'False'

  --with-baseline[:<committish>]      EXPERIMENTAL: Use results stored in
                                      stryker dashboard to only test new
                                      mutants. | default: 'False'


Reporting options:
  -o|--open-report[:<report-type>]    When this option is passed, generated
                                      reports should open in the browser
                                      automatically once Stryker starts testing
                                      mutants, and will update the report till
                                      Stryker is done. Both html and dashboard
                                      reports can be opened automatically. |
                                      default: 'Html' | allowed: Html, Dashboard

  -r|--reporter                       Reporters inform about various stages in
                                      the mutation testrun. | default:
                                      ['Progress', 'Html'] | allowed: All,
                                      Progress, Dots, ClearText, ClearTextTree,
                                      Json, Html, Dashboard, RealTimeDashboard,
                                      Markdown, Baseline, Gitlab

  -v|--version                        Project version used in dashboard reporter
                                      and baseline feature. | default: ''

  --dashboard-api-key                 Api key for dashboard reporter.

  --azure-fileshare-sas               A Shared Access Signature for Azure File
                                      Storage is required when Azure File
                                      Storage is used for dashboard compare. For
                                      more information:
                                      https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/storage/common/storage-sas-overview
                                      | default: ''

  --s3-bucket-name                    The name of the S3 bucket to store
                                      baseline reports in. Required when the S3
                                      baseline provider is selected. | default:
                                      ''

  --s3-endpoint                       Custom endpoint URL for S3-compatible
                                      storage (e.g. MinIO, Backblaze B2).
                                      Optional; when not set the default AWS S3
                                      endpoint is used. | default: ''

  --s3-region                         The region for the S3 bucket (e.g.
                                      us-east-1). Optional; when not set the SDK
                                      resolves the region from environment
                                      variables or profile. | default: ''

  -O|--output                         Changes the output path for Stryker logs
                                      and reports. This can be an absolute or
                                      relative path.


Misc options:
  --skip-version-check                Skips check for newer version. | default:
                                      false

  --break-on-initial-test-failure     Instruct Stryker to break execution when
                                      at least one test failed on initial run. |
                                      default: 'False'

  --diag                              Stryker enters diagnostic mode. Useful
                                      when encountering issues.
                                      Setting this flag makes Stryker increase
                                      the debug level and log more information
                                      to help troubleshooting. | default:
                                      'False'

  -t|--test-runner <vstest,mtp>       Specify the test runner to use. | default:
                                      'vstest' | allowed: vstest, mtp


Commands:
  init                                

Run 'Stryker [command] -?|-h|--help' for more information about a command.
Welcome to Stryker for .Net! Run dotnet stryker to kick off a mutation test run
